Subject: [PATCH] Limit Liuqin DisplayPort lanes by the Type-C assignment

Expose the four routed lanes in the board graph and keep the OEM HBR2
ceiling. The QMP mux already distinguishes DP-only C/E assignments from
shared D/F assignments. Clamp the sink capabilities to the applied mux
mode before advertising modes and recheck the assignment at PHY power-on.
Start each AUX session with provisional two-lane RBR options.

 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts |  3 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c                  |  6 ++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c               |  3 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c                 | 22 +++++++++++++--
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.h                 |  4 ++-
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c         | 34 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 66 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
index 643435f..9b9c8b7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
@@ -1232,7 +1232,8 @@
 };
 
 &mdss_dp0_out {
-	data-lanes = <0 1>;
+	data-lanes = <0 1 2 3>;
+	link-frequencies = /bits/ 64 <1620000000 2700000000 5400000000>;
 };
 
 /*
